<!--
  aihu-waitlist-form — styled recipe (Phase 2, performativeUI port Slice 7 —
  docs/plans/2026-08-01-performative-ui-port.md §Tier-B batch 3).

  Design and behavior transcribed in spirit from performativeUI (MIT); no
  source text or `pui-` class names vendored — see NOTICES.md.

  An email-capture form with an inline success state after submit.

  NO NETWORK LOGIC HERE — submitting dispatches `waitlist-submit` (detail
  `{ email: string }`, bubbles, composed) and swaps to the success message;
  the consumer owns the actual request (and can call `setAttribute('submitted',
  '')` — see below — or just let the component's own optimistic swap stand,
  their call).

  DESIGN DECISION — inline state swap, NOT a popover. The roadmap flags this
  as "overlay-dependent"-adjacent and floats a popover for the success state,
  but a form's own success message is not a disclosure over something else —
  it doesn't need `role="dialog"`, positioning, outside-dismissal, or any of
  the overlay primitive's machinery. A `<group if=...>` swap between the form
  and a `role="status"` message is the honest, simpler surface: it works with
  zero JS beyond the swap itself, needs no z-index/portal reasoning, and reads
  correctly to a screen reader via the SAME live-region mechanism a toast
  would use anyway. Building the popover-backed version here would be pure
  ceremony over a plain "swap this text" requirement.

  DESIGN DECISION — plain native `<input type="email">` / `<button>`, NOT the
  registry's `input`/`button` recipes and NOT `@aihu/primitives/input` +
  `@aihu/primitives/form-control`. Three reasons: (1) the registry's OWN
  `input.aihu` recipe is itself just a styled native `<input>` wrapper with NO
  `$extends` ("the native control plus light DOM is enough for forms" — see
  its header) — reusing it here would add a cross-recipe dependency for zero
  behavioral gain over writing the same native element locally; (2)
  `@aihu/primitives/input`'s `AihuInput` registers under the SAME default
  `aihu-input` tag the registry's `input.aihu` recipe also compiles to — a
  real double-registration collision the moment both are loaded together (the
  same hazard `chat-fab.aihu`'s header documents for popover), avoidable
  entirely by not registering a custom element for the field at all; (3) a
  single email field needs exactly the a11y that a real `<label>` WRAPPING a
  real `<input>` already gives it for free (implicit label association, no id
  bookkeeping) — `@aihu/primitives/form-control`'s slotted `aria-describedby`/
  `for` wiring solves a harder problem (multi-piece coordination) this
  single-field form doesn't have.

  No `submitting` signal: there is no real async operation in this component
  (the actual network call is the consumer's job, wired off `waitlist-submit`)
  — the form→success swap is synchronous, so there is no in-flight window a
  disabled/submitting state would ever cover. `disabled` IS supported (a
  consumer showing their OWN pending state can set it) — forwarded to both the
  input and the submit button.

  `shadow: 'light'` — see the parent execution plan's theming decision.

  REAL DEFECTS FOUND AND WORKED AROUND, not framework fixes in scope for this
  slice:

  1. A bare `required` attribute (no `={...}`) on a template element compiles
     to the static primitive `required: ''` (`packages/arbor/src/attrs.ts`
     `_setAttrOrProp`'s "static primitive" path). Because `'required' in
     HTMLInputElement.prototype` is true, that path assigns the DOM PROPERTY
     (`el.required = ''`), and `required` is a boolean IDL attribute — `''`
     coerces to `false`, so the constraint SILENTLY NEVER APPLIES. Every other
     boolean-property attribute in this registry (`disabled`, `checked`, …) is
     always bound through a real `prop()` boolean (`disabled={disabled}`),
     which never hits this trap — `required` is only ever written here as a
     literal `required={true}` for exactly that reason.
     (`cookbook/form-validation.aihu` has the same bare-`required` shape and
     is very likely affected too, but fixing a cookbook doc is out of scope
     here.)

  2. `ref={...}` on an element inside a `<group if=...>` populates its signal
     LATE — through a SEPARATE `onMount` the compiler registers only once the
     conditional branch is actually grown, not the synchronous ref-before-
     onMount assignment `before-after.aihu`'s header documents for an
     UNconditional top-level ref. A first attempt put `ref={formEl}` on the
     `<form>` itself (which only exists while `!submitted`) and read it back
     in an `effect()` — in principle reactive-enough to attach once the ref
     lands, but it never actually did (empirically verified with a direct
     `dispatchEvent(new Event('submit', {cancelable:true}))` probe:
     `defaultPrevented` stayed `false` no matter what). Root-caused as a real,
     narrow gap in this specific ref-inside-`<group if>`-plus-`effect()`
     combination — not a framework fix in scope here. WORKED AROUND instead by
     moving `ref={containerEl}` to the ALWAYS-PRESENT outer `<div>` (never
     conditional, so it gets the proven synchronous top-level-ref path) and
     listening for `submit` there: the event BUBBLES up from the
     conditionally-rendered `<form>` through the light-DOM tree regardless
     (`shadow: 'light'` has no real ShadowRoot to stop it), so a single
     container-level listener sees every submit without ever needing a ref
     into the conditional branch at all.
-->

@state {
  import { cn } from '@aihu/css-engine/runtime/cn'

  shadow: 'light'

  let label = prop({ default: 'Email' })
  let placeholder = prop({ default: 'you@example.com' })
  let buttonLabel = prop({ default: 'Join the waitlist' })
  let successMessage = prop({ default: "You're on the list — we'll be in touch." })
  let disabled = prop({ default: false })

  let containerEl = state(null)
  let submitted = state(false)

  onMount(() => {
    if (!containerEl) return
    const container = containerEl
    const onSubmit = (ev) => {
      const form = ev.target
      if (!(form instanceof HTMLFormElement)) return
      ev.preventDefault()
      const input = form.querySelector('input[type="email"]')
      const email = input ? input.value.trim() : ''
      if (!email) return
      submitted = true
      container.dispatchEvent(
        new CustomEvent('waitlist-submit', {
          detail: { email },
          bubbles: true,
          composed: true,
        }),
      )
    }
    container.addEventListener('submit', onSubmit)
  })
}

@template {
  <div ref={containerEl} data-slot="waitlist-form" class={cn('aihu-waitlist-form')}>
    <group if={!submitted}>
      <form class="aihu-waitlist-form-form">
        <label class="aihu-waitlist-form-label">
          <span class="aihu-waitlist-form-label-text">{label}</span>
          <input
            type="email"
            class="aihu-waitlist-form-input"
            name="email"
            placeholder={placeholder}
            required={true}
            disabled={disabled}
            autocomplete="email" />
        </label>
        <button type="submit" class="aihu-waitlist-form-submit" disabled={disabled}>
          {buttonLabel}
        </button>
      </form>
    </group>
    <group if={submitted}>
      <p class="aihu-waitlist-form-success" role="status">{successMessage}</p>
    </group>
  </div>
}

@style {
  .aihu-waitlist-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    max-width: 24rem;
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-label {
    display: flex;
    flex: 1 1 12rem;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-label-text {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-input {
    height: 2.25rem;
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
    background-color: var(--color-background);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    transition: border-color 0.15s, box-shadow 0.15s;
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-input::placeholder {
    /* --color-muted-foreground is the packs' lowest-contrast text token
       (3.14-3.35:1 against this input's --color-background across all four
       pack x mode combos — fails AA's 4.5:1 floor everywhere) — the same
       failing token commits 2362b5ea/bc0b0a59 systematically removed from
       every other registry component. --color-secondary is the same house
       remedy those commits used for this exact token on prompt/mock-ide/
       pricing-card's placeholder-shaped text: 6.39-7.23:1 here, comfortably
       AA in all four combos (see this component's PR for the hand
       computation against packages/css-engine/styles/aihu-default.css /
       aihu-graphite.css). */
    color: var(--color-secondary);
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-input:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--color-ring);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-ring) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-input:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-input:invalid:not(:placeholder-shown) {
    border-color: var(--color-destructive);
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-submit {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 2.25rem;
    padding-inline: 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-primary-foreground);
    background-color: var(--color-primary);
    border: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: filter 0.15s;
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-submit:hover {
    filter: brightness(1.06);
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-submit:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-ring);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-submit:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .aihu-waitlist-form-success {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    /* `--color-success-foreground` is a solid-fill pairing (cream-on-green) —
       wrong ink for a light TINTED background. `color-mix` toward
       `--color-foreground` is the same tinted-surface pattern
       `eyebrow-pill.aihu`'s `tone="success"` rule uses. */
    color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-success) 60%, var(--color-foreground));
    background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-success) 12%, transparent);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-success);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
}
